  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday) \nIssued at 1017 PM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe rest of the week and the upcoming weekend should feature\nbenign fall weather. An upper low will track across the TX \nPanhandle Thurs AM, resulting in a weak sfc low (MSLP around \n1008mb) bringing a renewed push of northerly winds in its wake. \nPrecip chances with this wave appear minimal, owing to limited \nmoisture return ahead of it. Forecast soundings show a brief \nwindow early Thurs AM where there may be sufficient saturation for\nlight rain, but outside of that the soundings appear too dry. \nEnsemble guidance is not bullish about the rain chances, keeping \nthem below mentionable levels for now. High temps during the long \nterm forecast period will generally be a tad below normal, in the \nupper 50s to mid 60s, with the exception of Wednesday which looks \na bit warmer relative to Thurs- Sun. Low temps will be near \nnormal, ranging from the upper 30s to mid 40s. A hard freeze still\nappears unlikely through at least the upcoming weekend.",
